    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An excellent opportunity to acquire a three-bedroom semi-detached bungalow with extended kitchen to the rear, detached block garage and shed with a large gated side entrance. Nestled in a lovely mature development within stone's throw of Castle pollard town now serviced with the New TFI Local Link 818 Mullingar to Castlepollard via Collinstown, offering 5 daily return services Monday to Thursday, 8 on Friday, 7 on Saturday and 5 on Sundays.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises of the entrance hall, sitting room with Pellet stove and front aspect. Three bedroom all with laminate flooring, fully tiled wet room and kitchen with fitted wall and floor unit to the rear.\n\nThe exterior of this home has a lovely mature garden to the front with a host of shrubberies, walled in boundary and double gates to the driveway lead to the detached garage.\n\nWithin striking distance of Castlepollard town centre which offers all necessary amenities including a selection of local shops, pubs, Hotel, coffee shop, Churches, Tesco shopping centre, Gym, two primary schools and a post primary school.\n\nEasy access of many lakes and rivers for water sport and fishing enthusiasts, Tullynally Castle garden and forestry walks on your door step. Lough Lene Blue Flag Lake in Collinstown is less than a 10-minute drive famed for fishing, swimming and water sports. Castlepollard is a key location for access in travel to Dublin on the M50 approx. 40 mins, Mullingar approx. 12km, other key routes include Athlone, Tullamore and Galway.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nFront Hall 1.025m x 1.710m (3'4\" x 5'7\"):\nPVC door, tiled flooring\n\nBedroom One 3.156m x 4.680m (10'4\" x 15'4\"):\nDouble room, front aspect, laminate flooring\n\nSitting Room 3.255m x 4.879m (10'8\" x 16'):\nCarpet flooring, pellet stove heats water and radiators, front aspect\n\nKitchen 2.641m x 4.564m (8'8\" x 15'):\nRear aspect, tiled flooring, tiled splashback, fully fitted kitchen wall and floor units\n\nBedroom Two 2.693m x 3.753m (8'10\" x 12'4\"):\nDouble room, front aspect, laminate flooring\n\nBedroom Three 2.410m x 2.685m (7'11\" x 8'10\"): Laminate flooring, single room, rear aspect, stira to attic\n\nBack Hall 1.827m x 1.622 (6' x 1.622):\nTiled flooring, PVC door to rear\n\nWet Room 2.670m x 1.642m (8'9\" x 5'5\"):\nFully tiled, WC, wash hand basin, Triton Novel SR electric shower, heated towel rail\n\nDouble Shed 8.452m 4.676m (27'9\" 15'4\"):\nBlock built, power supply, concrete base\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n-Oil Fired Central Heating\n-Concrete yard\n-Pellet stove in sitting room\n-PVC double glazed windows and doors\n-Private rear garden\n-Outside tap\n-Detached garage and fuel shed\n-Side entrance with concrete yard offering ample car parking space\n-Walking distance to town centre Mature gardens Mains water Mains drainage\n-Built circa 1956\n\nIncluded in Sale\n-Dishwasher\n-Fridge\n-Gas cooker\n-Washing machine\n-Kitchen cabinet\n-Blinds\n-Couch\n-Free standing wardrobe\n\nBER Details\nBER Rating: D2\nBER No. 119343283\n\nDirections\nFrom the Square in Castlepollard, proceed out Water Street and take the left turn just after the Primary school, continue to the first right and take the next left and No.17 is on the right-hand side as indicated by our Sherry FitzGerald For Sale Board. Eircode N91 VF10"
      },
